+## Subtopics
+
+### Uniform Grid for Reflection Rays
+A uniform grid in object space used to handle reflection rays, as perspective grids are not useful due to lack of coherence and preferred direction [S2]. Rays traverse the uniform grid by walking from one voxel to another using a voxel walk procedure [S2]. Each ray independently computes the next voxel starting with the starting point, loads triangles of the encountered voxel, and checks intersection until the first intersection is found [S2]. This method is simple but assumes no coherence between rays, which can incur a heavy penalty on older GPUs with large SIMD width and no caching to exploit access locality [S2]. Choose this variant when tracing reflection rays in dynamic scenes where perspective grids fail to provide traversal coherence [S2].
+
 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity:** $O(K \cdot S)$ per pixel, where $K$ is the number of GI samples (`VOXEL_GI_SAMPLES`) and $S$ is the maximum DDA steps (`VOXEL_GI_STEPS` or `VOXEL_REFL_STEPS`) [S1, unofficial].
